Package: TweetScraperR
Type: Package
Title: Collect Posts and User Data from 'X' (Formerly 'Twitter')
Version: 0.8.1.9000
Authors@R: c(
    person(given = "Agustín", family = "Nieto",
           email = "agustin.nieto77@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person(given = "vladkens", role = c("ctb", "cph"),
           comment = "Author of 'twscrape'; the account pool logic is ported from it, see inst/COPYRIGHTS")
    )
Description: Collects posts, user profiles, lists, followers and related
    metadata from the social network 'X' (formerly 'Twitter') and returns
    them as tidy data frames. Data are retrieved through a local 'Node.js'
    engine that drives a 'Chromium' browser with 'Playwright', reusing the
    sessions of the user's own accounts. Work can be distributed across
    several accounts of the user while respecting the per-endpoint rate
    limits reported by 'X'; the design of this account pool is ported from
    the 'Python' library 'twscrape' <https://github.com/vladkens/twscrape>.
    Also includes helpers to plot word, emoji and time frequencies, and
    optional sentiment and image analysis through the 'OpenAI' API.
    Documentation is written in Spanish.
URL: https://github.com/agusnieto77/TweetScraperR, https://agusnieto77.github.io/TweetScraperR/
BugReports: https://github.com/agusnieto77/TweetScraperR/issues
